```c
/*
 * isr_ring.c - Lock-free ISR/thread ring buffer for Zephyr RTOS
 *
 * Single-producer / single-consumer (SPSC) ring buffer:
 *   - Producer: ISR context only (isr_ring_write / isr_ring_write_byte)
 *   - Consumer: thread context only (isr_ring_read / isr_ring_read_byte)
 *
 * Design
 * ------
 * Two monotonically increasing (mod 2^N) indices, head (next write)
 * and tail (next read), are held as atomic_t. The fill count is
 * head - tail (unsigned wraparound arithmetic), so the head==tail case
 * is unambiguous, the whole capacity is usable, and no per-slot
 * bookkeeping is needed.
 *
 * Since exactly one context ever writes each index, only a single-word
 * atomic load/store (which is naturally atomic on all Zephyr-supported
 * architectures) plus an arch_mem_fence() to order the buffer data
 * accesses are needed. There are no locks, no allocation, no blocking
 * calls, and the producer never waits -- if the buffer is full, the
 * overflow bytes are dropped and the number of bytes actually stored
 * is returned. FIFO order is preserved.
 *
 * Memory ordering:
 *   Producer: data stores -> arch_mem_fence() -> atomic_set(head)
 *   Consumer: atomic_get(head) -> arch_mem_fence() -> data loads
 *             -> arch_mem_fence() -> atomic_set(tail)
 */
```

